Focused CLI tests passed, including a race-enabled run. The delivery parser test, build, and focused vet checks also passed. The full validation attempts were interrupted after the sandbox refused new build directories. The artifact check was stopped because its success path refreshes the delivery index. No repository changes or attestation were made.

Rules applied during review: mixed Go feature and documentation change; review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style, delivery-evidence, and knowledge-governance rules. No UI or infrastructure rules applied.

Removing the unavailable-binding rejection appears consistent with R2: `material_clean` independently witnesses the validated head, while an uncomputable spec binding remains unavailable. The remaining explicit assumption is that module input declarations are accurate.

